# 必考词 Unit19
# 领域: 考研
# 学科: 英语词汇
# 来源: 2025红宝书考研英语词汇
# 描述: 必考词Unit19核心词汇

{{renew}}{{/rɪˈnjuː}}{{v. 更新； renew；续签}}{{I need to renew my passport before it expires.}}
{{renovate}}{{/ˈrenəveɪt}}{{v. 翻新； renovate；修复}}{{The old building was renovated into a modern office.}}
{{reputation}}{{/ˌrepjuˈteɪʃn}}{{n. 名声； reputation；声誉}}{{The company has a reputation for quality products.}}
{{request}}{{/rɪˈkwest}}{{n./v. 请求； request}}{{She submitted a request for a transfer.}}
{{require}}{{/rɪˈkwaɪər}}{{v. 需要； require；要求}}{{The job requires a lot of patience.}}
{{rescue}}{{/ˈreskjuː}}{{v./n. 营救； rescue}}{{The firefighters rescued the child from the burning building.}}
{{resemble}}{{/rɪˈzembl}}{{v. 像； resemble；类似于}}{{She resembles her mother in many ways.}}
{{resent}}{{/rɪˈzent}}{{v. 怨恨； resent；对…不满}}{{He resented being treated unfairly.}}
{{reserve}}{{/rɪˈzɜːv}}{{v./n. 保留； reserve；储备}}{{I'd like to reserve a table for two.}}
{{reside}}{{/rɪˈzaɪd}}{{v. 居住； reside；存在于}}{{The family resides in a quiet suburb.}}
{{resign}}{{/rɪˈzaɪn}}{{v. 辞职； resign；使顺从}}{{He resigned from his position as CEO.}}
{{resist}}{{/rɪˈzɪst}}{{v. 抵抗； resist；抵制}}{{The soldiers resisted the enemy attack.}}
{{resolve}}{{/rɪˈzɒlv}}{{v./n. 决心； resolve；解决}}{{They resolved the dispute through negotiation.}}
{{resource}}{{/rɪˈsɔːs}}{{n. 资源； resource}}{{The country is rich in natural resources.}}
{{respond}}{{/rɪˈspɒnd}}{{v. 回应； respond；回答}}{{She responded quickly to the emergency.}}
{{restore}}{{/rɪˈstɔːr}}{{v. 恢复； restore；修复}}{{The government aims to restore public confidence.}}
{{restrain}}{{/rɪˈstreɪn}}{{v. 抑制； restrain；限制}}{{He had to restrain his anger.}}
{{restrict}}{{/rɪˈstrɪkt}}{{v. 限制； restrict；约束}}{{Access to the building is restricted.}}
{{retain}}{{/rɪˈteɪn}}{{v. 保留； retain；保持}}{{The company retained its top talent with bonuses.}}
{{retreat}}{{/rɪˈtriːt}}{{v./n. 撤退； retreat； retreat}}{{The army was forced to retreat.}}
{{retrieve}}{{/rɪˈtriːv}}{{v. 检索； retrieve；取回}}{{You can retrieve the data from the database.}}
{{reveal}}{{/rɪˈviːl}}{{v. 揭示； reveal；透露}}{{The investigation revealed the truth about the scandal.}}
{{revenue}}{{/ˈrevənjuː}}{{n. 收入； revenue；税收}}{{The company's revenue increased by 15% this year.}}
{{reverse}}{{/rɪˈvɜːs}}{{v./adj./n. 颠倒； reverse；相反的}}{{The court reversed the decision of the lower court.}}
{{revise}}{{/rɪˈvaɪz}}{{v. 修订； revise；修改}}{{The report has been revised to include new data.}}
{{revive}}{{/rɪˈvaɪv}}{{v. 复兴； revive；恢复}}{{The government tried to revive the struggling economy.}}
{{revolution}}{{/ˌrevəˈluːʃn}}{{n. 革命； revolution；旋转}}{{The industrial revolution transformed society.}}
{{rhetoric}}{{/ˈretərɪk}}{{n. 修辞； rhetoric；花言巧语}}{{His speech was full of empty rhetoric.}}
{{rigid}}{{/ˈrɪdʒɪd}}{{adj. 严格的； rigid；僵硬的}}{{The rules are too rigid to allow any flexibility.}}
{{rival}}{{/ˈraɪvl}}{{n./v. 竞争对手； rival；与…匹敌}}{{The two companies have been rivals for years.}}
{{robust}}{{/rəʊˈbʌst}}{{adj. 强健的； robust；坚固的}}{{The economy showed robust growth last quarter.}}
{{role}}{{/rəʊl}}{{n. 角色； role；作用}}{{Education plays a crucial role in personal development.}}
{{rotate}}{{/rəʊˈteɪt}}{{v. 旋转； rotate；轮换}}{{The Earth rotates on its axis.}}
{{rough}}{{/rʌf}}{{adj. 粗糙的； rough；大致的}}{{The road was rough and difficult to drive on.}}
{{routine}}{{/ruːˈtiːn}}{{n./adj. 日常的； routine；惯例}}{{Exercise has become part of my daily routine.}}
{{ruin}}{{/ˈruːɪn}}{{v./n. 毁灭； ruin；废墟}}{{The scandal ruined his political career.}}
{{sacrifice}}{{/ˈsækrɪfaɪs}}{{v./n. 牺牲； sacrifice；献祭}}{{She sacrificed her career to raise her children.}}
{{sample}}{{/ˈsɑːmpl}}{{n./v. 样品； sample；品尝}}{{The survey was based on a sample of 1000 people.}}
{{sanction}}{{/ˈsæŋkʃn}}{{n./v. 制裁； sanction；批准}}{{The UN imposed sanctions on the country.}}
{{satellite}}{{/ˈsætəlaɪt}}{{n. 卫星； satellite}}{{The satellite provides data for weather forecasting.}}
{{saturate}}{{/ˈsætʃəreɪt}}{{v. 使饱和； saturate；浸透}}{{The market is saturated with cheap imports.}}
{{scale}}{{/skeɪl}}{{n./v. 规模； scale；攀登}}{{The project is on a large scale.}}
{{scandal}}{{/ˈskændl}}{{n. 丑闻； scandal}}{{The politician was involved in a corruption scandal.}}
{{scarce}}{{/skeəs}}{{adj. 稀缺的； scarce；不足的}}{{Clean water is scarce in many parts of the world.}}
{{schedule}}{{/ˈʃedjuːl}}{{n./v. 时间表； schedule；安排}}{{The meeting is scheduled for 3 p.m.}}
{{scheme}}{{/skiːm}}{{n./v. 计划； scheme；图谋}}{{The government launched a new housing scheme.}}
{{scope}}{{/skəʊp}}{{n. 范围； scope；机会}}{{The scope of the investigation has been expanded.}}
{{scrutiny}}{{/ˈskruːtəni}}{{n. 审查； scrutiny；仔细检查}}{{The report was subject to intense scrutiny.}}
{{sector}}{{/ˈsektər}}{{n. 部门； sector；领域}}{{The private sector plays a major role in the economy.}}
{{secure}}{{/sɪˈkjʊər}}{{adj./v. 安全的； secure；获得}}{{The building is secured with cameras and guards.}}
{{segment}}{{/ˈseɡmənt}}{{n. 部分； segment；片段}}{{The company targets a specific market segment.}}
{{seize}}{{/siːz}}{{v. 抓住； seize；没收}}{{Police seized a large quantity of illegal drugs.}}
{{select}}{{/sɪˈlekt}}{{v. 选择； select；选拔}}{{She was selected to represent the school.}}
{{semester}}{{/sɪˈmestər}}{{n. 学期； semester}}{{The fall semester begins in September.}}
{{seminar}}{{/ˈsemɪnɑːr}}{{n. 研讨会； seminar}}{{The professor held a seminar on climate change.}}
{{senior}}{{/ˈsiːniər}}{{adj./n. 高级的； senior；年长者}}{{She is a senior manager at the company.}}
{{sensitive}}{{/ˈsensətɪv}}{{adj. 敏感的； sensitive；灵敏的}}{{The issue is very sensitive and must be handled carefully.}}
{{sequence}}{{/ˈsiːkwəns}}{{n. 顺序； sequence；序列}}{{Please arrange the events in chronological sequence.}}
{{session}}{{/ˈseʃn}}{{n. 会议； session；一段时间}}{{The training session lasted for two hours.}}
{{setback}}{{/ˈsetbæk}}{{n. 挫折； setback}}{{The project suffered a major setback.}}
{{settle}}{{/ˈsetl}}{{v. 解决； settle；定居}}{{They settled the dispute out of court.}}
{{severe}}{{/sɪˈvɪər}}{{adj. 严重的； severe；严厉的}}{{The storm caused severe damage to the coast.}}
{{shallow}}{{/ˈʃæləʊ}}{{adj. 浅的； shallow；肤浅的}}{{The river is too shallow for boats.}}
{{shelter}}{{/ˈʃeltər}}{{n./v. 庇护所； shelter；躲避}}{{The building provides shelter for the homeless.}}
{{shift}}{{/ʃɪft}}{{v./n. 转移； shift；转变}}{{There has been a shift in public opinion on the issue.}}
{{shrink}}{{/ʃrɪŋk}}{{v. 收缩； shrink；减少}}{{The economy shrank by 2% last year.}}
{{signal}}{{/ˈsɪɡnl}}{{n./v. 信号； signal；表明}}{{The company sent a positive signal to investors.}}
{{significance}}{{/sɪɡˈnɪfɪkəns}}{{n. 重要性； significance；意义}}{{The discovery has great significance for medical research.}}
{{simultaneous}}{{/ˌsɪmlˈteɪniəs}}{{adj. 同时的； simultaneous}}{{The two events were almost simultaneous.}}
{{skeptical}}{{/ˈskeptɪkl}}{{adj. 怀疑的； skeptical}}{{Many scientists are skeptical about the findings.}}
{{skip}}{{/skɪp}}{{v. 跳过； skip；略过}}{{You can skip the introduction and go straight to Chapter 2.}}
{{slight}}{{/slaɪt}}{{adj. 轻微的； slight； slight}}{{There was a slight improvement in her condition.}}
{{slim}}{{/slɪm}}{{adj./v. 苗条的； slim；微小的}}{{The chances of success are very slim.}}
{{snap}}{{/snæp}}{{v./n. 折断； snap；快照}}{{The branch snapped under the weight of the snow.}}
{{soar}}{{/sɔːr}}{{v. 飙升； soar；翱翔}}{{Temperatures soared to record highs.}}
{{sole}}{{/səʊl}}{{adj./n. 唯一的； sole；鞋底}}{{She is the sole survivor of the crash.}}
{{solemn}}{{/ˈsɒləm}}{{adj. 庄严的； solemn；严肃的}}{{The ceremony was a solemn occasion.}}
{{solid}}{{/ˈsɒlɪd}}{{adj./n. 固体的； solid；坚固的}}{{The house is built on solid foundations.}}
{{sophisticated}}{{/səˈfɪstɪkeɪtɪd}}{{adj. 复杂的； sophisticated；老练的}}{{The system uses sophisticated technology.}}
{{source}}{{/sɔːs}}{{n. 来源； source；源头}}{{What is the source of this information?}}
{{span}}{{/spæn}}{{n./v. 跨度； span；持续}}{{The bridge spans the river.}}
{{spark}}{{/spɑːk}}{{v./n. 引发； spark；火花}}{{The debate sparked a national conversation.}}
{{specialize}}{{/ˈspeʃəlaɪz}}{{v. 专门从事； specialize}}{{She specializes in corporate law.}}
{{species}}{{/ˈspiːʃiːz}}{{n. 物种； species}}{{Many species are endangered due to deforestation.}}
{{speculate}}{{/ˈspekjuleɪt}}{{v. 推测； speculate；投机}}{{Analysts speculated about the future of the market.}}
{{sphere}}{{/sfɪər}}{{n. 领域； sphere；球体}}{{She works in the sphere of international relations.}}
{{spill}}{{/spɪl}}{{v./n. 溢出； spill；泄露}}{{Oil spilled into the sea from the damaged tanker.}}
{{spin}}{{/spɪn}}{{v./n. 旋转； spin；纺纱}}{{The earth spins on its axis.}}
{{spirit}}{{/ˈspɪrɪt}}{{n. 精神； spirit；灵魂}}{{The team showed great spirit during the competition.}}
{{spite}}{{/spaɪt}}{{n. 恶意； in spite of；尽管}}{{In spite of the difficulties, they succeeded.}}
{{sponsor}}{{/ˈspɒnsər}}{{n./v. 赞助者； sponsor；赞助}}{{The event was sponsored by a major corporation.}}
{{spot}}{{/spɒt}}{{n./v. 地点； spot；发现}}{{This is a great spot for a picnic.}}
{{squeeze}}{{/skwiːz}}{{v./n. 挤压； squeeze；压缩}}{{She squeezed the tube of toothpaste.}}
{{stable}}{{/ˈsteɪbl}}{{adj./n. 稳定的； stable；马厩}}{{The patient is now in a stable condition.}}
{{staff}}{{/stɑːf}}{{n./v. 员工； staff；配备人员}}{{The hospital is understaffed.}}
{{stake}}{{/steɪk}}{{n. 利害关系； stake；赌注}}{{He has a personal stake in the outcome.}}
{{stale}}{{/steɪl}}{{adj. 不新鲜的； stale；陈旧的}}{{The bread has gone stale.}}
